# The Charas Ball -- nine pinches rolled together.
#
# Redrawn 2026-09-14. Generated art, not Warlon Mhite's hand: edit freely.
#
# Charas is rubbed off a living plant and rolled between the palms, never pressed, so the surface is
# hand-worked: a few soft creases, each with a lit lip below it, and glossy specks where rolled resin
# picks up a sheen. A first draft with more creases read as cracked rock. Block contrast, but
# near-black needs a little more room at the top or the ball reads as a hole in the world.
#
# The model is three intersecting boxes with auto-UVs, so every face samples a different part of
# this texture -- it has no composed centre, and tiles.

@palette ball
. = none
2 = 120E0A      a crease
3 = 211912      the body
4 = 2E2419
5 = 3A2E20
6 = 5A4631      a glossy speck
7 = 7E664A

@texture block/charas_ball 16x16 type=block tiling=true palette=ball
